# No nested `if`

Do not write an `if` block inside another `if` block.

Prefer, in order:

1. **Guard clauses** — validate and `return` / `throw` / `continue` before the main path.
2. **Boolean locals** — name the condition, then one top-level `if`.
3. **Extract a function** — when a branch needs async work or several steps.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
if (dto.email !== undefined) {
  if (email !== user.email) {
    if (existing && existing._id !== user._id) {
      throw new ConflictException('...');
    }
  }
}

// ✅ GOOD
if (email === user.email) {
  return;
}
const takenByOther = existing !== null && String(existing._id) !== String(user._id);
if (takenByOther) {
  throw new ConflictException('...');
}
```

`else if` chains and single-level `if` / `else` (siblings, not nesting) are fine.
